  "solution": {
    "text": "Given that $f(x)$ is an odd differentiable function.\r\nThen, $f(-x)=-f(x)$\r\n$\\begin{array}{lr}\\Rightarrow & -f^{\\prime}(-x)=-f^{\\prime}(x) \\\\ \\Rightarrow & f^{\\prime}(-x)=f^{\\prime}(x)\\end{array}$\r\nPut $x=3$ in Eq. (i), we get\r\n$\\therefore$\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\nf^{\\prime}(-3)=f^{\\prime}(3) \\\\\r\nf^{\\prime}(-3)=2\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$",
